 },
 "coldArrival": {
  "concern": "Task 26 left the cold arrival frames at 33.3 ms, 0.7 ms under the 34 ms gate, and asked that the new framing not push them over.",
  "found": "On the first build of the framing (99e90c7; its runs are not kept in the repo) the phone's arrival frame was 50 ms in 6 of 6 cold runs (phone-cpu4 and phone-dpr3-cpu4, at 617 ms into the pass, scroll 392 to 396; recorded in the traces: the box's first frame on screen carried a 9 ms resize and repaint of the dot field's canvas); desktop was 33.4 ms (no step). Cause: the box framing follows the camera, a phone's shelf starts at its left end (initialCamX = -maxX) but the prefit framed the row with the camera at 0, so the dot field's region (dotRegion, which depends on where the row is) was another size at the first frame on screen and the canvas was resized and repainted in it.",
  "fixed": "R55.3n: the camera goes to where a run starts (homeCamera) before the prefit frames the row, and again in start() before its framing (one reframe, not two). The arrival frame is 33.3 ms again (two vsyncs): phone-cpu4 33.4, 33.4, 33.3; dpr 3 33.4, 33.3, 33.4; desktop-cpu4 33.3 to 33.4 (one run 50 ms inside a hero change window); gate not widened."
 },
 "heroChangeBoxOnScreen": {
  "base": "docs/redesign/compare/round7/r55-hero-change-base.json (6f98c1c, the same tool, 3 runs): desktop-cpu4 box on screen worst 33.3 ms, 0 over 34 ms, 2 over 20 ms; phone-cpu4 worst 16.8, 0 over 34, 0 over 20",
  "head": "this file (the holds of the three runs of each profile, first attempts): desktop-cpu4 box on screen, frames inside the change windows: worst 16.8, 0 over 34, 0 over 20 (3 runs, 1374 frames); phone-cpu4: worst 16.8, 0, 0 (1688 frames); phone-dpr3-cpu4: worst 16.8, 0, 0 (1749 frames); desktop-cpu1: worst 16.8, 0, 0",
  "verdict": "no worse than the base on both profiles (worst frame and counts of frames over 34 and over 20 ms all no more than the base's). The one 66.7 ms frame in desktop-cpu4 run 1's hold was outside every change window (above) and did not repeat."
 },
